From: RISE Project <info@riseproject.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] postprocess-binary: skip local symbols in the export check

library_symbols() takes field 6 of every `objdump -T` line that mentions
.text, assuming each one is an exported symbol of the form
`addr flags type .text size version name`. On RISC-V, binutils' ld always
keeps a local section symbol for .text in .dynsym (it is there in every
riscv64 shared library, e.g. Rocky 10's own libzstd.so.1), which objdump
prints with one field fewer:

  0000000000024a10 l    d  .text	0000000000000000              .text

so the list comprehension raises IndexError on libopenslide.so.1 and the
bdist build stops. Local symbols are never exports, so skip them.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [riscv64 is not an upstream openslide-bin platform yet]

--- a/artifacts/postprocess-binary.py
+++ b/artifacts/postprocess-binary.py
@@ -35,7 +35,13 @@
         out = subprocess.check_output(
             [os.environ['OBJDUMP'], '-T', file]
         ).decode()
-        return [line.split()[6] for line in out.split('\n') if '.text' in line]
+        return [
+            line.split()[6]
+            for line in out.split('\n')
+            # skip local symbols, such as the .text section symbol that
+            # RISC-V linkers add to .dynsym
+            if '.text' in line and line.split()[1] != 'l'
+        ]
     elif host == 'darwin':
         out = subprocess.check_output(
             [os.environ['DYLD_INFO'], '-exports', file]
